    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5925" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφίλεκτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>spoken both ways:</i>
			hence, <i>doubtful,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ὢν κράτει</span>
			<i>questioned</i> in his title to rule, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				1585
			</span></i>; <i>involving dispute,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔρις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					500
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Th.</u>
					800
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>double,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πήματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					881
				</span></i>
			.</div>
